1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,463
Nolawi! Delina! Come down here!

2
00:00:03,513 --> 00:00:09,354
Every Sunday morning, it starts the same
way: my mom's voice, from downstairs.

3
00:00:09,458 --> 00:00:12,068
Whatever the week was, we come down.

4
00:00:14,458 --> 00:00:17,040
Downstairs, the coffee has already
begun.

5
00:00:19,458 --> 00:00:23,948
The beans crackle in the pan, and the
smell climbs the stairs before we do.

6
00:00:25,458 --> 00:00:29,415
Etan smoke curls through the room.
Nobody is in a hurry.

7
00:00:30,958 --> 00:00:35,472
There's popcorn, sometimes kolo, and a
lot of noise.

8
00:00:35,958 --> 00:00:42,812
With the first cup, abol, we catch up on
the week: school, tests, work.

9
00:00:42,917 --> 00:00:48,279
With the second, tona, it's university
applications, and everyone has an

10
00:00:48,329 --> 00:00:49,330
opinion.

11
00:00:49,458 --> 00:00:54,541
The third cup is bereka, the blessing.
The room gets quieter.

12
00:00:54,958 --> 00:00:57,437
The coffee was never really the point.

13
00:00:58,083 --> 00:01:03,698
It's the few hours every week we're all
in the same room. Next Sunday, she'll

14
00:01:03,748 --> 00:01:06,502
call again, and we'll come down.

